This is a pre-release of the ESZ/ZAP toolkit, version 2.2c.

Contents
--------

* ESZ -- a typechecker for Z and the ESPRESS notation mSZ, which includes 
  generation of HOL-Z theories and generation of the Java-based 
  intermediate Z representation ZIRP

* ZAP -- a compiler for a functional sublanguage of Z

* ZIRP -- classes and API documentation

* ESZ Emacs/XEmacs mode -- a mode for operating
  ESZ and ZAP from within Emacs

* VTeX XEmacs mode -- a mode for visualising Z and LaTeX under XEmacs

* esz.sty -- a LaTeX style for Z and the ESPRESS notation mSZ


[Documentation is not complete, this will be the main task to do
for the final release 2.2c!]

It is recommended to operate ESZ and ZAP from
within the ESZ emacs mode, and follow the online documentation
(menus). To start the ESZ mode, run M-x esz under
Emacs.

For installation instructions, see the file INSTALL.








